<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Revenue attribution</h2>
<p>For each revenue attribution journey, record message purpose, channel permission or other applicable basis, evidence source, and the current recipient state. Enrollment is not dispatch clearance: recheck suppression, matching cart and order, subscription, refund and support-case state immediately before sending, including queued retries. Required order and service messages need their own purpose-limited route; optional care and editorial marketing still need eligibility.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Hold optional marketing unless an applicable basis is evidenced; send only necessary service through its eligible route</td><td>An order or email address alone does not establish marketing permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Check current permission for this purpose and channel before educational marketing</td><td>Permission for one channel or purpose does not cover every journey</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Recheck matching-cart status and applicable recovery eligibility at dispatch; withhold discounts initially</td><td>A cart event alone does not authorize a reminder</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Exit recovery for the matching cart; route required service separately and assess later optional care on its own eligibility</td><td>Purchase ends the obsolete reminder, not every future eligible message</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Hold conflicting promotions while the case is unresolved; preserve necessary case updates</td><td>Case closure alone does not establish marketing eligibility</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Use a documented inactivity policy with clicks, purchases and reliable signals; do not classify by non-opens alone</td><td>Open tracking is incomplete and is not a permission record</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Verify current SMS permission, purpose, suppression, applicable quiet hours and caps</td><td>Email permission cannot substitute for SMS permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Check the named recipient, account role, channel basis and applicable agreement</td><td>B2B status alone neither grants permission nor proves a contract breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Apply proportionate validation using actual address and abuse evidence</td><td>A free domain alone does not establish poor quality or ineligibility</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Revenue Attribution QA profiles excluded from reporting</td><td>Revenue Attribution test sends skew attribution reads</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Document any evidence-based exception, owner, reason and expiry</td><td>Inferred identity alone does not justify an undocumented exception</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Hold marketing while provenance is unresolved; use repermission only through an already permitted route</td><td>A repermission email is itself a message requiring eligibility</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Revenue attribution</h2>
<p>Attributed revenue is not profit for revenue attribution. A self-funding revenue attribution program survives a full cost model: subscription, contact or send overages, SMS credits, capture tooling, templates, agency time, and every point of revenue attribution discount margin. For revenue attribution, a stack at fifteen percent of attributed margin needs simplification first, optimization second.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. For revenue attribution, free plans always bind somewhere; identify whether contacts, sends, branching, or support caps your revenue attribution motion first.</p>
