<ol>
<li>Lock revenue attribution flow edits a full fortnight before peak.</li>
<li>Revenue Attribution QA spans purchase, refund, and case paths.</li>
<li>Revenue Attribution guardrails must exit matching-cart recovery for fresh buyers while preserving required service and separately eligible later messages.</li>
<li>Plan revenue attribution holdout size around the predefined outcome, power and uncertainty; keep required service in both optional-marketing arms.</li>
<li>Set revenue attribution SMS boundaries ahead of volume.</li>
<li>For revenue attribution, test tier limits against peak projections.</li>
<li>For revenue attribution, name a daily inbox-health monitor.</li>
<li>Pre-write revenue attribution rollback moves per flow before launch.</li>
</ol>
<p>For revenue attribution, schedule quarter-one review before the first send. Writing revenue attribution suppression rules, discount caps, and escalation paths down in week one saves weeks of peak-season triage and hands newcomers a working revenue attribution playbook.</p>
<p>Close each revenue attribution quarter with a written ledger — revenue attribution sends shipped, suppressions honored, margin retained, failed bets — so revenue attribution vendor decisions rest on one shared evidence file, not scattered memory.</p>
